{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115824",
      "title": "Configuring Component Inputs & Outputs",
      "lectureOrder": 146,
      "videoOrder": 138,
      "sourceHash": "9d6f1c5bca25aad81ed7c4ad5cb03e3cb53d535e904e738859add3d1cd8849f7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 2.49,
          "en": "Now at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.49,
          "end": 5.49,
          "en": "we're almost done with this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.49,
          "end": 9.15,
          "en": "but of course this section was never primarily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.15,
          "end": 10.74,
          "en": "about this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.74,
          "end": 14.28,
          "en": "Instead, it's about diving deeper into components, templates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.28,
          "end": 16.14,
          "en": "and related features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.14,
          "end": 20.37,
          "en": "and there still are some features that should be covered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.37,
          "end": 23.55,
          "en": "For example, if you are dealing with inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.55,
          "end": 27.15,
          "en": "and outputs, you got some configuration options here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.15,
          "end": 28.8,
          "en": "which you should know about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.8,
          "end": 32.4,
          "en": "And when using that input function, you can set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 35.943,
          "en": "that configuration by passing an object to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.336,
          "end": 39.3,
          "en": "though only if you have required here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.3,
          "end": 41.7,
          "en": "Otherwise, that would be the default value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.7,
          "end": 44.82,
          "en": "So then you should actually pass the configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.82,
          "end": 46.563,
          "en": "as a second value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.61,
          "end": 51,
          "en": "With required, there is no default value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51,
          "end": 54.573,
          "en": "so then you only pass the configuration object to input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.47,
          "end": 59.19,
          "en": "If you're using @input, so this decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.19,
          "end": 62.31,
          "en": "then the configuration object is passed directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.31,
          "end": 64.203,
          "en": "to that input decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.82,
          "end": 69.09,
          "en": "Now, what can you configure here though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.09,
          "end": 73.26,
          "en": "Well, you can, for example, set an alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.26,
          "end": 75.48,
          "en": "and that does what the name implies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.48,
          "end": 78.93,
          "en": "It allows you to change the name of the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.93,
          "end": 82.74,
          "en": "If, for some reason, you want to use data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.74,
          "end": 84.69,
          "en": "as a name in this ticket component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.69,
          "end": 87.66,
          "en": "but some other name outside of this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.66,
          "end": 89.37,
          "en": "you could do this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.37,
          "end": 91.2,
          "en": "I could, for example, set this to data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.2,
          "end": 92.973,
          "en": "and rename this here to ticket.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.82,
          "end": 98.52000000000001,
          "en": "Now I would have to change it in the template as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.52000000000001,
          "end": 102.36,
          "en": "but since I'll revert back soon, I'll not do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.36,
          "end": 105.50999999999999,
          "en": "But with that, we would now still use data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.50999999999999,
          "end": 110.50999999999999,
          "en": "as a input name in the place where we're binding the input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.15,
          "end": 112.47,
          "en": "but inside of the component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.47,
          "end": 114.363,
          "en": "we would be using this property name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.77000000000001,
          "end": 118.35,
          "en": "Now, I'll go back to using data internally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.35,
          "end": 120.63,
          "en": "and to not using an alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.63,
          "end": 124.65,
          "en": "because it's actually not recommended to use an alias.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.65,
          "end": 127.62,
          "en": "You should only do that if you have a good reason",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.62,
          "end": 129.36,
          "en": "for going for this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.36,
          "end": 132.51,
          "en": "since it otherwise can cause some confusion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.51,
          "end": 135.33,
          "en": "Another configuration setting you have here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.33,
          "end": 138.483,
          "en": "is that you can set up a transform function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.32,
          "end": 142.5,
          "en": "So you can set up that transform option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.5,
          "end": 145.53,
          "en": "and provide a function as a value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.53,
          "end": 148.77,
          "en": "and that function will get the input value as an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.77,
          "end": 152.25,
          "en": "and can then return a transformed value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.25,
          "end": 153.15,
          "en": "You could, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.15,
          "end": 155.79,
          "en": "use that to perform some cleanup work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.79,
          "end": 159.36,
          "en": "or to change the type of the input value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.36,
          "end": 161.94,
          "en": "though you also should be careful with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.94,
          "end": 163.14,
          "en": "and you should make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.14,
          "end": 165.84,
          "en": "that you are not performing any transforms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.84,
          "end": 167.31,
          "en": "that could make the usage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.31,
          "end": 170.103,
          "en": "of this component confusing or unclear.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.15,
          "end": 172.5,
          "en": "Here, I don't need that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.5,
          "end": 175.95,
          "en": "but it's worth knowing about these different features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.95,
          "end": 178.65,
          "en": "that you can set up such a transformer function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.65,
          "end": 181.173,
          "en": "and that you can assign an alias.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.4,
          "end": 183.96,
          "en": "And for output it's similar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.96,
          "end": 187.5,
          "en": "You can also pass a configuration object to output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 187.5,
          "end": 190.53,
          "en": "and of course also to the output decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 190.53,
          "end": 192.96,
          "en": "Though here it's actually only an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 192.96,
          "end": 194.97,
          "en": "if you're using the output function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 194.97,
          "end": 199.56,
          "en": "because you only have one option here, you can set an alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 199.56,
          "end": 201.84,
          "en": "just as you could for the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 201.84,
          "end": 203.97,
          "en": "to give this event a different name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 203.97,
          "end": 206.793,
          "en": "outside of this component than inside of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 207.84,
          "end": 209.52,
          "en": "For the output decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 209.52,
          "end": 212.16,
          "en": "you therefore just directly pass the alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 212.16,
          "end": 214.353,
          "en": "as a value to @Output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 216.84,
          "end": 221.01,
          "en": "Now with that, we would listen to closeTicket here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 221.01,
          "end": 225.21,
          "en": "instead of close, if that is the alias we assign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 225.21,
          "end": 230.01,
          "en": "Now, I will go back to close again and not assign that alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.01,
          "end": 232.62,
          "en": "because it's also discouraged for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 232.62,
          "end": 235.35,
          "en": "but you should know about these options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.35,
          "end": 237.48,
          "en": "and that's why I mentioned them here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 237.48,
          "end": 241.02,
          "en": "that you can set up transformer functions for inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 241.02,
          "end": 244.533,
          "en": "and aliases for both inputs and outputs.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
